@page "/about"

<PageTitle>About · Juris</PageTitle>

<section class="j-hero">
    <div class="j-container">
        <div class="j-eyebrow">About Juris</div>
        <h1>The Legal Intelligence Hub.</h1>
        <p class="j-lede">
            Juris is a data-driven career and media platform for Ontario law students and junior legal professionals — a single source of truth for firms, law schools, recruitment, and the conversations that shape early careers.
        </p>
    </div>
</section>

<section class="j-section">
    <div class="j-container" style="max-width: 760px;">
        <div class="j-prose">
            <h2>Why we exist</h2>
            <p>Most career intelligence in legal Canada lives in PDFs, viewbooks, and locker-room conversation. We made it a website. The rule is simple: every datapoint a 1L through articling student needs to make a deliberate career decision should be one click away — without a paywall.</p>

            <h2>What we cover</h2>
            <p><strong>Firms.</strong> Every major Ontario law firm has a profile. Hard data on the left — articling salary, class size, hireback rate, billable target, recruitment deadlines. The Vibe on the right — editorial reviews, AI policies, work-life balance, perks.</p>
            <p><strong>Schools.</strong> Every Ontario law school in one comparison matrix — tuition, median LSAT and GPA, employment outcomes at nine months, Seven-Sisters hire rate. Plus deep-dive profiles on mooting, clinics, and Pre-Law pathways.</p>
            <p><strong>Recruitment.</strong> A live feed of every OCI, articling, 2L summer, and 1L deadline that matters. Status pills, countdowns, direct apply links.</p>
            <p><strong>News.</strong> Careers, Market News, Student Life, and "The Vault" — anonymous voices from inside the recruit.</p>

            <h2 id="partner">For firms</h2>
            <p>Verified firms claim editorial control of their profile and access the <a href="/verified">HR Dashboard</a> — anonymized analytics on which schools are reading, which perks they are clicking, how their engagement compares to peers, and where students are dropping off. The dashboard is the renewal driver.</p>

            <h2 id="contact">Contact</h2>
            <p>Editorial: <a href="mailto:editorial@juris.local">editorial@juris.local</a></p>
            <p>Partners (firm verification): <a href="mailto:partners@juris.local">partners@juris.local</a></p>

            <h2 id="privacy">Privacy</h2>
            <p>We collect newsletter signups and anonymized analytics events (university affiliation, year of study, page interactions). Personal email addresses are never shared with firms. IP addresses are hashed at ingestion. You can unsubscribe and delete your data at any time by emailing us.</p>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>
